{#
  MY WORK — Figma 184:13749. The three featured case studies.

  THE ONE DARK BAND on the page, and the inversion lives entirely in the .work
  scope in tokens.css — this file and _work.css never name a colour.

  Renders the FEATURED projects that have card copy, which is the three written
  case studies. WOW Global is featured but has no case study and no `card`, so
  it filters out here rather than being special-cased in the template: when its
  write-up lands, adding a `card` block to projects.js is the whole change.

  The heading is the site's two-tone pattern — regular word, bold word — the
  same shape as the hero's "I'm Pari." and About's "About Me".
#}

{% from "components/project-card.njk" import projectCard %}

<section class="work" id="featured-works">
  <div class="work__inner">
    <h2 class="work__heading">
      <span class="work__heading-lead">{{ work.heading.lead }}</span>
      <span class="work__heading-rest">{{ work.heading.rest }}</span>
    </h2>

    <div class="work__rows">
      {%- for p in collections.workCards %}
        {{ projectCard(p, loop.index) }}
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
